B.2. Design Rationale
AI-Work composes four modular design choices—client-side scoring, reputation updating, job–worker matching, and skill
dynamics—each chosen for economic plausibility and tractability.
Client-side scoring.
For a job J and bidding agent i, let qi,J,t = Ri,τ(J),t denote the agent’s public reputation on the
job’s task and let xi,J,t = pi,J,t/bt(J) denote the bid normalized by the posted budget. We use a CES scoring family,
