where Pi,t = [(J1, pi,J1,t), . . . , (Jℓ, pi,Jℓ,t)], ℓ≤L,
(TRAIN, k)
where k ∈T .
If the agent bids, Pi,t is a strict preference ordering over the submitted jobs. Each agent can ultimately be allocated at most
ν jobs per round.
Observation to the LLM agent.
At each round, agent i receives a structured observation containing:
• Market history: the last Hctx rounds of allocations, showing for each matched job the job id, posted budget, winning
agent id, and the winner’s reputation on that job’s task (displayed on a 5-star scale).
• Leaderboard: the current public cumulative earnings ranking.
21

