At each environment step, agents compete for control through an auction (Figure 2). Given the current
observation ot, each agent evaluates its triggering predicate to determine eligibility. The eligible set
is Et = {a ∈Pe : ϕa(ot) = 1}. If Et = ∅, no agent acts and the episode terminates or defaults to a
null transition, depending on the environment. Otherwise, the auction winner is the highest-bidding
eligible agent, a⋆
