C.4
Bucket-brigade payments recover structured credit assignment
Bucket-brigade payments also provide a mechanism for assigning credit to earlier agents. The next
two results show that, under additional structure, the payment received from the next winner can be
interpreted as either a Bellman continuation value or an ordered marginal contribution in a workflow.
Proposition 1 (Bellman-like credit under continuation pricing). If the expected payment received
from the next winner equals the discounted continuation value,
E[Yt | ht, a⋆
