Lemma 3 (Extinction of externally loss-making collusions). Let S be a coalition of agents that may
coordinate bids, prompts, and internal transfers. If every nonempty surviving sub-coalition T ⊆S
has strictly negative expected aggregate external wealth drift on recurrent episode segments, then all
agents in S are removed in finite time almost surely.
Proof of Lemma 3. Consider the currently surviving colluding set T ⊆S. By assumption, whenever
T is active on recurrent episode segments,
E[∆WT (τ) | Fτ −] ≤−ηT
for some ηT > 0. The increments are bounded, so the coalition wealth WT has strictly negative
